<v SPEAKER_07>mayor sirachi Thank You council president on July 14th the house appropriations subcommittee will meet to mark up the transportation housing and urban development bill and that will go to full committee on July 17th at the federal level president trump is proposing a full cut of the cdbg that's the community development block grant and home programs the 2025 cdbg allocation to the city is 1.4 million and for context the county also receives a block grants about twice that and over the last five years cdbg funding to the city of lancaster was 7.7 million dollars this year as was presented to council earlier this year these funds support a wide variety of efforts they support city services to maintain quality affordable housing promote neighborhood quality of life through property maintenance inspections and education police social workers the health and housing social worker some of our neighborhood engagement efforts some of our streetscape improvement efforts and critical repair grants to residents which have assisted over 300 homes it also provides the required match for our hud led remediation grants to leverage this funding and this funding also supports our partners in the work that they do to support housing case management affordable housing rehabilitation and economic development and organizations such as tenfold south and concern neighbors sacca and partners with purpose home funding provides critical funding for new affordable housing and rehabilitation of city homes for affordable housing and over the past four years the city has received 1.6 million in home entitlement funds which have supported organizations such as chestnut housing hdc mid-atlantic landis communities and sacca eliminating these programs as is being proposed by the trump administration would remove nearly 1.5 million dollars annually that flows into the city of lancaster this reduction will also impact how the pennsylvania legislature prioritize funding and how dollars are allocated from the state to the city because there are a lot of crossover points between federal state and local funds and of course the state budget hasn't yet been finalized and so we're we're collectively bracing um this is in the scheme of the work that we do a very small amount of money 1.5 million dollars for CDBG 1.6 million dollars in home funding and you know we we have been very fortunate that we have received additional federal funding in the past that has made larger scale affordable projects happen for the first time in 40 to 50 years in the city like the HDC project for example on College Avenue with 64 units but without this money there would be nothing in terms of an investment that the city would be able to make in supporting the issue that is on everyone's mind which is the affordability of housing and so I want to just thank Rebecca guys are here who's who is here tonight for her and her and the team within CPAD to pull this there's a more robust data sheet that is being prepared to share with Senator Congressman Smucker's office and I am encouraging counselors to reach out to Congressman Smucker as well as anybody who's listening tonight to both appreciate CDBG investments for the over the last 50 years and to highlight the ways in which these dollars are utilized in our community both CDBG and home and if you want to talk about something specific and you need some data to strengthen your case statement drop me a message and we will help you in your advocacy next I want to provide a brief update related to an email that I received last week from our police social workers Kelly and grace a while ago we decided at the board of the trust and charities which is a very small fund to allocate about $10,000 annually to the police social workers because they routinely run into situations in which a little bit of money could make a very big difference in the lives of the residents that they are serving and so last week was the first time that they used the credit card that was attached to this account and through a combination of donations and purchases they acquired a bed a microwave and a mini fridge for an 82 year old gentleman who was doing very much without now he he has a bed to sleep on and a means to reheat and store food so they also connected him to Meals on Wheels so that he can be have access to reliable quality food to assist him in these basic necessities of life and so I'm really pleased that we found a way with a very small amount of money to help this gentleman and I also know that Kelly and Grace will use these funds to help folks like this gentleman who need a little extra help to meet some of their daily needs and to make their lives better thought you should all know that work is happening every day at our police bureau thank you mayor sirachi

